The call site is `this.camera()` inside `GameWorld.loadEnvironment(Environment env)`:

```java
// for the default camera we center the camera on the environment
if (this.camera().getClass().equals(Camera.class)) {
  camera().setFocus(env.getCenter());
}
```

`GameWorld.camera()` is:

```java
public ICamera camera() {
  return this.camera;
}
```

So nullability depends entirely on the field `this.camera`.

From the provided code:

- On game initialization (`Game.init`), a camera is explicitly created and set:

```java
world.setCamera(new Camera());
```

- `GameWorld.setCamera` is:

```java
public void setCamera(final ICamera cam) {
  if (this.camera() != null) {
    Game.loop().detach(camera);
  }

  camera = cam;

  if (cam != null && !Game.isInNoGUIMode()) {
    Game.loop().attach(cam);
    cam.updateFocus();
  }
}
```

